[CENTER]
[SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Leaf[/COLOR][COLOR=#2C3E50]RTP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#7F8C8D]Free Random Teleport (RTP) Plugin for Paper, Spigot, Folia, Fabric, NeoForge & Velocity[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[/CENTER]

[CENTER][I]Once upon a time, I wanted to explore a minecraft world. I asked for [/I]/rtp[I] in servers I played on. They told me "no, that's laggy", and I took that personally.[/I][/CENTER]

[B]Random teleport that's easy to set up, easy to tune, and fast.[/B] Drop the jar in and [I]/rtp[/I] works with zero config, tune it in-game with [I]/rtp menu[/I], or build on the public [I]rtp-api[/I], without the lag spike other random-teleport plugins cause.

[B]At a glance:[/B]
[LIST]
[*]🚀 [B]Plug-and-play:[/B] drop the jar in, type [I]/rtp[/I], done. Zero config.
[*]🛠️ [B]No YAML required:[/B] tune regions, safety, and effects in-game with [I]/rtp menu[/I].
[*]🧩 [B]One jar, every platform:[/B] build on the public [I]rtp-api[/I] and ship a single addon for all of them.
[*]⚡ [B]No "Finding a safe location..." wait:[/B] destinations are pre-verified off-tick, never on the main thread.
[*]📈 [B]Measured on a public harness:[/B] 19.8 TP/s on Paper, 4 ms worst tick (next-best: 70 ms).
[*]🛡️ [B]Audited safety:[/B] no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim bypass, no silent failures.
[/LIST]

[CENTER]
[I]Minecraft 1.20.x / 1.21.x / 26.x. Legacy Forge isn't native; run this jar under Arclight / Mohist.[/I]

[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#16A085]Trusted since 2021: 4.6 stars over 30+ reviews, 430k+ downloads.[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]Latest builds, Folia-tagged releases, and beta channels also live on [URL='https://modrinth.com/plugin/leafrtp']Modrinth[/URL][/B] (auto-updater and Pterodactyl friendly).[/SIZE]

[/CENTER]
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Why operators pick LeafRTP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[B]Everything below ships in the free build, no add-ons:[/B]

[LIST]
[*][B]12 claim integrations bundled[/B] (GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, WorldGuard, Towny, Lands, +7 more). No teleport into protected land.
[*][B]Vault economy:[/B] optional charge per teleport, per-region pricing, auto-refund on cancel.
[*][B]Effects engine:[/B] particles, sounds, fireworks, potions on every teleport phase.
[*][B]Per-player cooldowns & usage limits[/B] out of the box.
[*][B]PvP/combat-tag gate, PlaceholderAPI, live map heatmaps, multi-world overrides.[/B]
[*][B]Extend it without a fork:[/B] the [I]rtp-api[/I] hooks take one-line suppliers to veto destinations, charge economy, add placeholders, override the world border, gate combat, replace the bare [I]/rtp[/I] action, or build custom arrival platforms. The [URL='ADDON_LINK_TODO']rtp menu addon[/URL] does exactly this, swapping bare [I]/rtp[/I] for its own picker.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dailystruggle/RTP/V3/docs/assets/img/teleport_title.webp[/IMG]
[I]A real [I]/rtp[/I] landing: pre-verified destination served in [B]0 attempts, 49 ms[/B] (1 gametick) on Folia, no "Finding a safe location..." wait. The title, sound, and effects shown are fully configurable.[/I][/CENTER]

Performance is in the numbers, not the prose: on Paper, LeafRTP holds a 4 ms worst tick where the next-best plugin hits 70 ms. Full Paper/Spigot/Folia tables and methodology are in the benchmark section below; reproduce them on your own rig: [URL=https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/helpers/StressTestRTP][I]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/I][/URL]. (How each feature stays cheap: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/wiki/Architecture'][I]Architecture[/I][/URL].)

[SPOILER='🧪 Verification & sources']
Every number on this page is anchored in the repo:
[LIST]
[*][B]Reproducible benchmarks[/B] with raw CSVs and per-run analyses: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/helpers/StressTestRTP'][B]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/B][/URL]
[*][B]Requirements traced to tests:[/B] every requirement, including the safety prohibitions, has an implementing class and regression test: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/dev/TRACEABILITY.md'][B]TRACEABILITY.md[/B][/URL]
[*][B]Every design decision is documented:[/B] dated, linkable notes on why teleports are queued, how the Anvil pre-filter skips chunk loads, and more: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/docs/adr'][B]docs/adr/[/B][/URL]
[*][B]bStats[/B] enabled. Anonymous usage stats help prioritize platform work.
[/LIST]
[/SPOILER]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]See the engine work, and watch it live[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
LeafRTP isn't a black box. [I]/rtp scan[/I] paints region safety onto a real in-game map (green safe, red unsafe) [B]as it verifies it[/B], off-tick on every platform. [I]/rtp info[/I] reports live TPS/MSPT, heap, latency percentiles, and rejection causes, no metrics add-on needed.

[URL='https://youtu.be/Ftjy1zw_S04'][B]Watch the scan paint a region live (video)[/B][/URL]. Details: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/wiki/Scan-and-Spatial-Memory'][B]Scan & spatial memory[/B][/URL], [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/wiki/Diagnostics'][B]Diagnostics[/B][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#C0392B]Requirements[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Hard requirements. If any are a [B]no[/B], EssentialsX [I]/rtp[/I] or HuskHomes are fine alternatives.

[LIST]
[*]✅ [B]Java 21+[/B] (REQ-RTP-SYS-001, non-negotiable).
[*]✅ [B]Paper, Spigot, or a Bukkit-family fork[/B], or Fabric / NeoForge (1.21.x / 26.1.x). Arclight / Mohist for Forge bridges.
[*]✅ [B]Vault[/B] (optional) for the economy charge; dormant when not installed.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#16A085]Install (30 seconds)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [I]LeafRTP-x.y.z.jar[/I] into [I]plugins/[/I].
[*]Start the server. A [I]default[/I] region is generated for you.
[*]Type [B]/rtp[/B].
[*]Run [B]/rtp menu[/B] to browse regions, worlds, and configuration in-game (clickable book on Paper / Folia, chat-paginated fallback elsewhere).
[/LIST]

Tune [I]plugins/RTP/config.yml[/I] and [I]plugins/RTP/regions/*.yml[/I] later, via [I]/rtp menu[/I] or by editing the YAML directly. Full admin guide is auto-unpacked into [I]plugins/RTP/docs/[/I] on first run, and lives online at the [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md'][B]admin guide[/B][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SPOILER='Full free feature list (click to expand)']
[LIST]
[*]🌀 [B]Deterministic spiral selection:[/B] bounded math, no unbounded re-roll loops. Predictable on huge worlds.
[*]🧠 [B]Spatial memory that persists across restarts:[/B] LeafRTP [I]learns[/I] which sectors keep failing and stops trying them.
[*]⏱️ Most [I]/rtp[/I] calls serve instantly from a [B]pre-generated location queue[/B]: destinations are chunk-loaded and verified before you type the command.
[*]🛡️ [B]Safety pipeline:[/B] radius check, invulnerability timer, optional landing platform, movement / damage cancel timers, material allow/deny list.
[*][B]Optional PvP / combat-tag gate:[/B] off by default; when enabled, /rtp is refused or delayed for players who recently dealt or took PvP damage, so a teleport can't be used to escape a fight. Native combat tracking, with optional PvPManager / CombatLogX / Simple Combat Log integration.
[*]🏛️ [B]Per-region arrival schematics:[/B] drop a [I].schem[/I] named after a region into [I]plugins/RTP/schematics/[/I] and every teleport into that region pastes it (a lobby pad, arrival shrine, or custom platform) on the landing spot. Cross-platform Sponge [I].schem[/I], decoded in-house (no WorldEdit required), claim-aware and audited.
[*]🌍 [B]Per-region, per-world config:[/B] shapes (square / circle / rectangle), curve weighting, vertical adjustors, sky-light check, world overrides, hot-reloadable YAML.
[*]✨ [B]Effects on every lifecycle phase:[/B] particles, sounds, fireworks, potion, note effects via the in-tree [I]effects-api[/I], gated by [I]rtp.effects.<name>[/I] permissions.
[*]🔗 [B]Twelve claim-plugin integrations bundled:[/B] GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, TownyAdvanced, SaberFactions, FactionsBridge, HuskClaims, RedProtect, CrashClaim, KingdomsX, Residence.
[*]🧩 Iris, Terra, and custom datapack generators work out of the box, with modded biome IDs preserved. [B]PlaceholderAPI[/B] and [B]ProtocolLib[/B] are supported as optional soft-deps.
[*]💰 [B]Optional Vault economy:[/B] charge players per [I]/rtp[/I] with per-region price, [I]priceOther[/I], params/biome surcharges, and a balance floor ([I]economy.yml[/I]); cost refunded automatically on cancel or pipeline failure ([I]refundOnCancel: true[/I] default); dormant when Vault is not installed.
[*]🛠️ [B]Public [I]rtp-api[/I][/B]: same surface as Pro. Trigger LeafRTP from a GUI, NPC, or quest; build your own UX without forking.
[*]🧩 [B]Platform-agnostic addons:[/B] addons compile against [I]rtp-api[/I] only and load through the [I]RTPAddon[/I] ServiceLoader SPI, so one addon module runs unchanged on Spigot, Paper, Folia, Fabric, and NeoForge. Config, safety hooks, teleport-pipeline callbacks, and scheduling are reached through platform-neutral APIs; you only add a platform module when the addon opens a platform-native UI. See the bundled RTP_ExampleAddon.
[*]🗺️ [B]Live map / heatmap visualizations:[/B] [I]/rtp scan[/I] paints region safety state (green safe / red unsafe) onto a real held map item while the chat readout streams cps, land %, and ETA. Free on Paper, Spigot, Fabric, and NeoForge.
[*]📊 [B]Built-in runtime observability:[/B] [I]/rtp info[/I] reports TPS/MSPT (spark-enhanced when spark is installed), JVM heap, pipeline latency percentiles, generation success/failure breakdown, and a [I]/rtp info biomes[/I] player-occupancy leaderboard, no metrics add-on needed.
[*]🌐 [B]12 locales, parity-enforced:[/B] shipped locales are CI-verified so a translated server never silently falls back to English on a new key.
[*]📚 [B]Every feature's design is documented:[/B] the reasoning behind each capability and a requirements-to-tests trace, all public: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/dev/INDEX.md'][B]docs/dev/INDEX.md[/B][/URL].
[/LIST]

[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dailystruggle/RTP/V3/docs/assets/img/menu_1.png[/IMG] [IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dailystruggle/RTP/V3/docs/assets/img/menu_2.png[/IMG]
[I]The clickable [I]/rtp menu[/I] book UI: admin panel (left) and the in-game config-file browser (right), everything tunable without leaving the game.[/I][/CENTER]

