[/TABLE]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SPOILER='📊 Full benchmark vs. alternative random teleport plugins on Paper, Spigot, and Folia']
[I]Paper rows: 2 OPed clients spamming [I]/rtp[/I] back-to-back, queues enabled where the plugin offers them, cooldowns/delays zeroed. Folia run: 3 OPed clients, radius equalized to 4096 blocks, ~600 s per plugin.[/I]

[B]Confidence legend:[/B] 🧪 = measured locally · 📖 = read from plugin docs · ❓ = inferred from architecture.

[B]Metrics:[/B] Throughput (TP/s, higher better) · MSPT p99 (worst 1-in-100 main-thread tick in ms, lower better) · Min TPS (lowest TPS observed; 20.00 = no hiccup) · CPU / TP (main-thread CPU per successful teleport).

[B]Paper 1.20.1 / 1.21.11[/B] is the reference dataset. Eight plugins, same harness, same world, same two OPed clients.
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Plugin[/TH][TH]TP/s[/TH][TH]MSPT p99 (ms)[/TH][TH]Min TPS[/TH][TH]CPU / TP (ms)[/TH][TH]Success[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]🧪 LeafRTP[/B][/TD][TD][B]19.8[/B][/TD][TD][B]4[/B][/TD][TD][B]20.00[/B][/TD][TD][B]16.9[/B][/TD][TD][B]100 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 JakesRTP[/TD][TD]20.0[/TD][TD]70[/TD][TD]20.00[/TD][TD]26.0[/TD][TD]100 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 BetterRTP[/TD][TD]7.3[/TD][TD]852[/TD][TD]20.00[/TD][TD]53.6[/TD][TD]100 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 HuskHomes[/TD][TD]6.2[/TD][TD]372[/TD][TD]20.00[/TD][TD]52.2[/TD][TD]100 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 AdvancedRTP[/TD][TD]2.16[/TD][TD]2 100[/TD][TD]19.95[/TD][TD]92.1[/TD][TD]96.3 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 EzRTP[/TD][TD]1.76[/TD][TD]2 903[/TD][TD]19.95[/TD][TD]139.6[/TD][TD]100 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 AsyRTP[/TD][TD]1.67[/TD][TD]4 534[/TD][TD]19.95[/TD][TD]38.8[/TD][TD]100 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 EssentialsX [I]/tpr[/I][/TD][TD]0.96[/TD][TD]4 504[/TD][TD]19.95[/TD][TD]88.9[/TD][TD]75.9 % §[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

§ EssentialsX [I]/tpr[/I] is a teleport-[I]request[/I] command (handshake + accept), not a teleport-[I]do[/I] command; the harness's 5 s per-attempt deadline times out a fraction of the request-accept latencies. Numbers are dispatch-shaped, not plugin-broken.

[B]Spigot 1.20.1[/B]: Spigot's platform-wide chunk-gen ceiling caps everyone in the 1–1.5 TP/s range during the burst; the latency tail is what matters.
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Plugin[/TH][TH]TP/s[/TH][TH]MSPT p99 (ms)[/TH][TH]Min TPS[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]🧪 LeafRTP[/B][/TD][TD][B]1.52[/B][/TD][TD][B]3[/B][/TD][TD][B]6.4[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 JakesRTP[/TD][TD]1.04[/TD][TD]2 252[/TD][TD]7.5*[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 BetterRTP[/TD][TD]1.33[/TD][TD]3 790[/TD][TD]2.18[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 HuskHomes[/TD][TD]0.93[/TD][TD]4 939[/TD][TD]2.59[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]Folia 26.1[/B]: the free build alone, no Pro adapter; on Folia, throughput plus the server-emitted region watchdog are the discriminators (global MSPT is a single-region sample and not meaningful).
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Plugin[/TH][TH]TP/s[/TH][TH]CPU / TP (ms)[/TH][TH]Watchdog stalls[/TH][TH]Success[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]🧪 LeafRTP[/B][/TD][TD][B]12.5[/B][/TD][TD][B]4.15[/B][/TD][TD][B]0[/B][/TD][TD][B]100 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 EzRTP[/TD][TD]5.3[/TD][TD]6.34[/TD][TD]7 (one region 20.4 s)[/TD][TD]96.2 %[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

EzRTP's 7 watchdog stalls (one region unresponsive 20.4 s) are the server's own record of synchronous [I]World.loadChunk[/I] calls on region threads; LeafRTP issued none. For reference, the Pro Folia adapter cleared the same run at 13.5 TP/s. The shared [I]rtp-core[/I] engine, not a Pro-only adapter, carries the free build's Folia result.

[B]Architecture support matrix[/B] [I](Spigot / Paper-and-forks / Folia)[/I]
[LIST]
[*][B]LeafRTP[/B] — ✅🧪 Off-tick Anvil pre-filter · ✅🧪 Fully async via [I]getChunkAtAsync[/I] · ✅🧪 Region Scheduler + off-tick pre-filter, no 1-tick stalls
[*][B]BetterRTP[/B] — ⚠️📖 Sync chunk load on miss · ⚠️📖 No off-tick safety pre-filter · ✅🧪 Folia 1.21.11 functional, p99 ~1.2 s
[*][B]EzRTP[/B] — ❌🧪 [I]NoSuchMethodError[/I] on Spigot 1.20.1 (Paper-only API) · ✅🧪 Works on Paper, no off-tick pre-filter · ⚠️🧪 Folia: sync [I]World.loadChunk[/I] on region threads, 7 watchdog stalls, 20.4 s freeze
[*][B]AsyRTP[/B] — ❌🧪 Fails to enable on Spigot 1.20.1 (Paper-only API in [I]onEnable[/I]) · ✅📖 Paper · ✅📖 Folia
[*][B]SorekillRTP[/B] — ⚠️❓ Designed for Redis cross-server, not single-server perf · ⚠️❓ Same · ❓📖
[*][B]AdvancedRTP[/B] — ⚠️📖 Safety-first, sync chunk load · ⚠️📖 Same · ❌📖
[*][B]JakesRTP[/B] — ⚠️📖 Async via flag; 10-slot cache · ✅📖 Same · ❌📖 No Folia
[*][B]EssentialsX /rtp[/B] — ✅📖 Main-thread chunk load per candidate · ✅📖 Same · ❌📖
[*][B]HuskHomes RTP[/B] — ✅📖 Bundled with homes suite · ⚠️📖 Same · ✅🧪 Folia functional, p99 ~900 ms
[/LIST]

[B]Caveats.[/B] Small client counts only (2 on Paper, 3 on Folia; the number is a floor, not a ceiling); hardware, view distance, world state, and other plugins will move them. Paper rows are 2-client runs (LeafRTP reproduced n=2; others n=1 on a single rig); the Folia run used 3 clients and its EzRTP failure is corroborated by the server's own watchdog log, independent of the harness. Competitor plugins update frequently; corrections welcome via GitHub issue with a contradicting repro or doc link. This table measures performance only; feature breadth is not benchmarked here. LeafRTP ships the clickable GUI menu, Vault economy, the lifecycle effects engine, and twelve bundled claim integrations alongside these numbers. It does not trade features for speed.

Full methodology, raw CSVs, per-run analyses: [URL=https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/helpers/StressTestRTP][I]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/I][/URL]. Video benchmark of [I]/rtp[/I] on a custom world generator: [URL=https://youtu.be/V0NyNK9JydM]youtu.be/V0NyNK9JydM[/URL].

