[TD][I]rtp.onevent.*[/I][/TD]
[TD][I]false[/I][/TD]
[TD]Auto-RTP on join / firstjoin / respawn / changeworld / move / teleport[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]rtp.admin[/I][/TD]
[TD][I]op[/I][/TD]
[TD]All admin tooling (reload, config, scan, info)[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]rtp.*[/I][/TD]
[TD][I]op[/I][/TD]
[TD]Every subcommand[/TD]
[/TR]
[/TABLE]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='Configuration files at a glance']
LeafRTP splits configuration by concern under [I]plugins/RTP/[/I]. Every file is hot-reloadable ([I]/rtp reload <file>[/I]) and editable in-game via [I]/rtp config <file>[/I] or the clickable [I]/rtp menu[/I].
[TABLE]
[TR]
[TH]File[/TH]
[TH]Scope[/TH]
[TH]Example keys[/TH]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]config.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Core / global behavior, database, menu renderer[/TD]
[TD][I]teleportDelay[/I], [I]teleportCooldown[/I], [I]cancelDistance[/I], [I]menu.renderer[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]regions/<name>.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Per-region shape, radius, center, queue, price, gates[/TD]
[TD][I]shape[/I], [I]vert[/I], [I]radius[/I], [I]cacheCap[/I], [I]price[/I], [I]requirePermission[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]worlds/<name>.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Per-world region routing and overrides[/TD]
[TD][I]region[/I], [I]override[/I], [I]requirePermission[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]safety.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Block / biome safety filter (flat material names in free; tag/state grammar is Pro)[/TD]
[TD][I]unsafeBlocks[/I], [I]airBlocks[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]economy.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Optional Vault pricing (works in the free build)[/TD]
[TD][I]price[/I], [I]priceOther[/I], [I]biomePrice[/I], [I]balanceFloor[/I], [I]refundOnCancel[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]effects/<name>.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Lifecycle effects (particles, sounds, fireworks, potions)[/TD]
[TD]per-phase effect definitions[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]performance.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Tick budgets, queue caps, caches[/TD]
[TD][I]maxAttempts[/I], [I]syncAllottedTime[/I], [I]minTPS[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]integrations.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Claim-plugin reroll toggles[/TD]
[TD][I]rerollWorldGuard[/I], [I]rerollGriefPrevention[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]logging.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Log verbosity and channels[/TD]
[TD]logging toggles[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]metrics.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Runtime-health metrics[/TD]
[TD]metrics toggles[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]language.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Locale selection (works in the free build)[/TD]
[TD][I]language[/I][/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]messages.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]User-facing text (fully localizable, REQ-RTP-F-013)[/TD]
[TD]message templates[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]network.yml[/I][/TD]
[TD]Proxy / multi-server selector[/TD]
[TD][I]enabled[/I], transport settings[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][I]lang/**[/I][/TD]
[TD]Bundled translation packs[/TD]
[TD]per-locale value files[/TD]
[/TR]
[/TABLE]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='📚 Commands, placeholders, soft-deps']
[B]Commands[/B] (full reference: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md']admin guide[/URL])
[LIST]
[*][B]/rtp[/B]: teleport to the default region for your current world.
[*][B]/rtp [parameter]:[value][/B]: specify [I]region:[/I], [I]world:[/I], [I]player:[/I], or temporary overrides.
[*][B]/rtp reload[/B]: reload all configuration from disk.
[*][B]/rtp scan start|pause|resume|reset|cancel[/B]: pre-warm spatial memory by walking a region (renamed from [I]/rtp fill[/I] in 2.x). Demo: [URL=https://youtu.be/Ftjy1zw_S04]youtu.be/Ftjy1zw_S04[/URL].
[*][B]/rtp menu[/B]: interactive admin menu; book on Paper / Folia, chat-paginated fallback elsewhere. Hardened in [I]3.0.0-beta.3[/I].
[/LIST]

[B]PlaceholderAPI[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]%rtp_player_status%[/B]: idle, waiting, teleporting, …
[*][B]%rtp_total_queue_length%[/B], [B]%rtp_public_queue_length%[/B], [B]%rtp_personal_queue_length%[/B]
[*][B]%rtp_teleport_world%[/B], [B]%rtp_teleport_x%[/B], [B]%rtp_teleport_y%[/B], [B]%rtp_teleport_z%[/B]
[/LIST]

[B]Soft dependencies (all optional):[/B] Vault (for the optional economy charge), PlaceholderAPI, ProtocolLib. [I]PaperLib is no longer required.[/I]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='❓ FAQ']
[B]Q: How do I stop /rtp from lagging my server, and why is LeafRTP faster than other random teleport plugins?[/B]
A: Destinations are pre-verified and chunk-loaded into a queue before you type the command, so [I]/rtp[/I] serves instantly without loading chunks on the main thread. Persistent spatial memory skips known-bad ground, and an off-tick Anvil pre-filter rejects unsafe spots before any chunk loads.

[B]Q: Is LeafRTP complicated to set up, and does it have economy, a GUI, and particle effects?[/B]
A: No, and yes. It works zero-config out of the box; regions, safety, and effects are optional to tune later. The clickable menu, Vault economy, effects engine, heatmaps, and twelve claim integrations all ship in the free build.

[B]Q: Why is it called "LeafRTP" now instead of just "RTP"?[/B]
A: "RTP" is the generic term for random teleport, so the old name was nearly impossible to find. It collided with every other random-teleport plugin, command, and forum thread in search and marketplace indexes. "LeafRTP" is a distinct, indexable name that points unambiguously at this plugin while keeping the [I]/rtp[/I] command, [I]rtp-api[/I], config paths, and data files exactly as they were. Nothing changes for existing installs, only the public name.

[B]Q: Does it work with Iris / Terra / custom datapack generators?[/B]
A: Yes. Region files are read directly, so modded and namespaced biome and block IDs are preserved. No configuration needed.


[B]Q: I'm on NeoForge.[/B]
A: NeoForge is a first-class supported platform on Minecraft 1.21.x / 26.1.x. Just drop the mod in.

[B]Q: I'm on Forge.[/B]
A: Run [B]Arclight[/B] or [B]Mohist[/B] (officially supported) and use this jar. A native Forge adapter is not planned.

[B]Q: Memory and MSPT: should I worry?[/B]
A: LeafRTP trades a bounded amount of RAM (the queue, bounded by [I]cacheCap[/I]) for speed. TPS should not drop below ~19 from LeafRTP alone on a healthy server; MSPT spikes during new-area generation are expected. That's the cost of generating chunks, not RTP.

[B]Q: How do I report a bug?[/B]
A: GitHub issue with server version, LeafRTP version, platform, relevant config files, and the error log section. See the [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md']admin guide[/URL] for the full reproduction template.
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='📞 Community Support Policy (read before filing an issue)']
Support for the free build is [B]community-tier and best-effort[/B]. I ship fixes when properly-reported issues land. Respecting this is how the plugin stays fast and current.
[LIST]
[*][B]Support covers bugs and configuration questions,[/B] after you've read the admin guide.
[*][B]Bug reports need a reproduction:[/B] server version, LeafRTP version, platform (Spigot / Paper / fork), [I]config.yml[/I], [I]regions/[/I], [I]safety.yml[/I], and the relevant [I]server.log[/I] section. Reports without these are asked for them once, then closed.
[*][B]"It doesn't work" is not a bug report.[/B] Tell me what you did, what you expected, and what actually happened.
[*][B]Unsupported on the free tier:[/B] native Forge (use Arclight / Mohist), plugin conflicts I can't reproduce, general MC-server admin questions.
[*][B]Response time:[/B] no SLA on the free build. Critical safety issues jump the queue regardless.
[*][B]Feature requests[/B] via GitHub issues. Priority follows the published roadmap, not ticket volume.
[/LIST]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='⚠️ Known limitations']
[LIST]
[*][I]safety.yml[/I] accepts flat material names ([I]LAVA[/I], [I]MAGMA_BLOCK[/I], [I]CACTUS[/I], [I]FIRE[/I]). Block tag / state-predicate grammar and SQL/Redis shared-state backends are not part of this build. Unknown materials log one warning, never silently dropped.
[*]Edits to [I]safety.yml[/I] and biome filters do not yet invalidate the persisted shape cache. Workaround: [I]/rtp scan reset <region>[/I].
[*]Emergency landing platform default is now [I]platformRadius: -1[/I] (disabled). Set to [I]0[/I] or higher to restore legacy 2.x behavior.
[/LIST]
Live list: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/CHANGELOG.md#known-issues']CHANGELOG[/URL].
[/SPOILER]


